  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nAssemblies\n\nWe can visit your school to deliver a 20 minute assembly, suitable for KS1 & 2, called the Soldiers' Stories at a cost of £50 per assembly.\n\nThe assembly is a great opportunity for pupils to be introduced to the military life of the county; gaining an appreciation for the people and events that make up the museum's stories. We also offer two distinct assemblies that focus on Remembrance Day during Autumn and Holocaust Memorial Day in January;  helping you to commemorate these dates.\n\nAll our assemblies are delivered using a PowerPoint presentation with images, sounds and video clips.\n\nPlease contact us for further details or any questions you may have.\n\nPlease note travel costs may be added to the assembly booking.\n\nHMD & Remembrance Assemblies\n\nWe can visit your school to deliver a 20-minute assembly to help your students commemorate Remembrance Day and Holocaust Memorial Day.\n\nOur package includes:\n\nRemembrance Assembly - Our County, Our War\n\nAvailable for Key Stage One and Key Stage Two\n\nThis assembly offers a great opportunity for students to commemorate Remembrance Day in November. It introduces students to the military life of the county to gain an appreciation for the people and events behind remembrance.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\n To discover local stories of acts of service from men and women during the First World War\n To examine different ways to commemorate\n To reflect on the importance of remembrance today\n\nHolocaust Assembly - Naomi and Arthur: Letters from Liberation\n\nAvailable for Key Stage Three\n\nThe assembly brings to life the story of a Bergen-Belsen camp survivor, Naomi Kaplan, and camp liberator, Arthur Tyler. This story sets an example of compassion and survival during the Holocaust. This session helps students to commemorate Holocaust Memorial Day in January.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\n To understand the importance of remembering the Holocaust today\n To examine the lifelong impact of living through the Second World War, life afterward, and the significance of hearing survivors’ voices\n To promote a message of what a difference we can make in the world through kindness, integrity and acting when we can\n\nEach assembly costs £50 to deliver, plus travel costs from the museum to your school. All assemblies are delivered using a PowerPoint presentation with images and sounds. Please get in touch with us for further details.\n\nCONTACT US ABOUT YOUR SCHOOL ASSEMBLY\nYour Name\nYour Email\nYour School\nMessage\nContact Us\n\nAlternatively, you can contact the Museum Programme Officer on 01993 810 214\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
  "footerText": ""
